WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.068
-Welcome, everybody!

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:04.137
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.405
This is it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.773
We made it.

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:10.009
And even though I just got here,
I can already tell

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:12.312
you guys are way better
than last night's audience.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:16.715
Yeah. Absolutely.
Absolutely.

00:00:16.715 --> 00:00:18.284
And you're actually here
on a very special night,

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:21.587
because, guys, tonight
is our fifth anniversary.

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:23.256
That's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:26.893
♪♪

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.194
That's right.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.263
We launched the show
exactly five years ago,

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:33.565
and as of tonight,
we'll have made 1,022 episodes

00:00:33.565 --> 00:00:34.834
of "The Tonight Show."

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:38.771
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:38.771 --> 00:00:40.240
That's crazy, right?

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.474
I can't believe
that it's been five years.

00:00:42.474 --> 00:00:43.676
Can you believe that?

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:46.012
-Actually I can, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:48.247
-Thank you very much, Higgins.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.247 --> 00:00:49.449
Here's a fun fact.

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:52.318
Tarik, tell everyone
what you told me earlier.

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:53.319
Tarik?

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:55.688
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:59.492
Year six off to a great start.
Here we go.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:02.061
Can we try that again?
Dave, can we do it again?

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:03.730
-No problem, Jimmy.
-All right, thanks.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:07.667
I'm gonna go from the
"fifth anniversary" line, okay?

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:08.701
It's the magic of television,
guys.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.637
We'll edit this out.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:12.572
Guys, tonight
is our fifth anniversary.

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.906
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:19.879
♪♪

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.614
That's right!

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.649
We launched the show
exactly five years ago,

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:26.852
and as of tonight,
we will have done 1,022 episodes

00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:28.121
of "The Tonight Show."

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:31.557
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:32.725
And check this out.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:35.228
Tarik, tell the everyone
what you told me earlier.

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:40.199
-Uh, in dog years, we're
actually at 7,154 episodes.

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:42.502
-Wow!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:45.905
No wonder why I'm so tired.

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:47.474
Now let's get to some news here.

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:49.008
If you watched
the Oscars last night,

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:51.911
allow me to explain.
I'm what's called a host.

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:55.214
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:55.214 --> 00:01:57.817
That's right, last night
were the Academy Awards.

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.418
It's when Hollywood
gathers together

00:01:59.418 --> 00:02:01.554
to celebrate all
the incredible films nobody saw.

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:05.959
It's great.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:08.160
-These --
These are the jokes?

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.762
Unbelievable.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.563
-...limo saying, "I just want
to take another look at you."

00:02:11.563 --> 00:02:14.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.201
Of course, there were some
interesting winners last night.

00:02:16.201 --> 00:02:18.337
For example, the Oscar
for Best Animated Short

00:02:18.337 --> 00:02:21.607
Went to Kim Jong-un.
-Oh, really? Wow.

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:23.242
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:23.242 --> 00:02:24.277
Didn't even know
he was nominated.

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:25.978
-He's very animated.
-Wow.

00:02:25.978 --> 00:02:27.813
-Speaking of Kim Jong-un,
later this week,

00:02:27.813 --> 00:02:29.415
he's meeting
with President Trump.

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:31.183
They have a lot in common --
they inherited everything

00:02:31.183 --> 00:02:33.286
from their dads,
and they cut their own hair.

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:35.154
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:37.590
That's right --
Trump's going to Vietnam.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:41.026
-Does he look, uh...
puffy?

00:02:41.026 --> 00:02:43.663
-Too much salt.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:46.933
-Ow.
-The meeting's from...

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:48.935
-Let's get all the ramen
out of his office.

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:50.436
-...Trump and Kim Jong-un,
their translator

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.138
will just
slowly walk into the ocean.

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:55.642
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:57.343
But I really wish cameras
were allowed in the room

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.077
for that meeting,
'cause I'd love to see Trump

00:02:59.077 --> 00:03:01.547
try to say the phrase
"nuclear prolipf-- prolip --"

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:04.317
Oh, God.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:06.852
"Nuclear proliferation."
Sorry.

00:03:06.852 --> 00:03:08.587
Uh, I wish cameras were there,

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:09.989
allowed in the room
for that meeting, yeah,

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:11.523
'cause I'd love to see Trump
try to say the phrase

00:03:11.523 --> 00:03:13.259
"nuclear polar--"
I can't say it.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:15.762
[ Laughter ]
I can't say it.

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:17.363
How's he gonna say it
if I can't say it?!

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:18.497
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.497 --> 00:03:20.066
Cut that joke.
We don't need that joke.

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:21.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:22.835
Hey!
Uh...

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:24.670
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:26.906
Five years, five years, yeah.

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:30.009
Some entertainment news --
a new Jean-Claude Van Damme...

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.644
-This is
an old person to you, right?

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:32.845
This guy looks old?

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:34.380
-"We Die Young"
is about what'll happen

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.915
if Trump's meeting if
Kim Jong-un doesn't go well.

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:38.250
-At least he still
combs his hair with a sneaker.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.518
-Get this -- the AARP...

00:03:39.518 --> 00:03:40.586
-That's young.

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:43.189
-...reality show
called "Date My Grandma."

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:44.623
[ Audience groans ]

00:03:44.623 --> 00:03:46.292
Like "The Bachelorette,"
but instead of a fantasy suite,

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:49.429
they get a booth at Denny's.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:52.498
-Oh, my God. I hate myself
for writing that joke.

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:54.834
-Yeah, I think we all hate you
for writing that joke.

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:57.236
-Yeah. You should quit.
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:57.236 --> 00:03:59.037
-Hey, I saw that Facebook
recently celebrated

00:03:59.037 --> 00:04:00.272
its 15th anniversary.

00:04:00.272 --> 00:04:02.107
I can't believe
it's been around for so long.

00:04:02.107 --> 00:04:04.043
Do you remember what it was like
before Facebook?

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:05.311
You remembered
your friends' birthdays

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:09.181
'cause you actually cared.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:09.181 --> 00:04:11.150
Bang.
[ Rimshot ]

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:15.121
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:18.124
Before Facebook, you spent time
at work actually working.

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:19.892
[ Rimshot ]

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.727
Before Facebook,
the only way to find out

00:04:21.727 --> 00:04:24.030
your uncle was racist
was seeing him on Thanksgiving.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:27.200
[ Rimshot ]

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.734
Finally, you guys,
a new report found

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:31.537
that the New York Knicks
are the NBA's most valuable team

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:34.039
at $4 billion.
That's crazy.

00:04:34.039 --> 00:04:35.507
That's a billion dollars
for every game

00:04:35.507 --> 00:04:37.076
they've won this year.

